h address your potential to supervise undergraduates from all backgrounds), a CV, your undergraduate and graduate transcripts, representative research papers, and course syllabi and evaluations (if available) as well as contact information for three people who will provide letters of reference. Applications can be submitted to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/ with the review beginning on November 15, 2026, and continuing until filled. Please direct any questions to the department chair, Dr. Clayton Byers ( clayton.byers@trincoll.edu ). Trinity College is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Posting Number F00300 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3770 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Representative research papers Research Statement Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Sample syllabi Teaching evaluations summaries Additional Applicant Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
