    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/104": {
      "title": "Shuttle Driver",
      "description": "Department: Campus Safety Category: Student & Community Life JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College is seeking dependable and safety-minded individuals to join our transportation team as a Campus Shuttle Driver. This role supports the campus community by providing safe, reliable, and courteous transportation for students. This is a part-time position with benefits. Schedule & Hours • Monday – Friday: 5:00 p.m. – 11:00 p.m. • Hours: May vary based on campus needs, special events, and the academic calendar. • Additional Hours: Occasional weekend or special-event hours may be available as needed. Trinity College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, wellness, dental and vision, retirement savings with employer match, flexible spending and health savings accounts, disability and life insurance; paid leave and other paid time off benefits; tuition benefits for employees and their dependents; and a variety of other employer-sponsored and voluntary fringe benefit programs. The anticipated annual base salary hiring range for this position is $16.94 to $19.38 per hour, with final placement determined by experience, skills, qualifications, and internal equity considerations. High School Diploma, or GED License: Must possess a valid U.S. Driver’s License (Class D/Standard). If operating a 12 passenger van a F endorsement is needed. Driving Record: Must have a clean driving record with no moving violations within the past three years. Experience: At least 3 years of licensed driving experience is preferred. Local Area Knowledge: Familiarity with the Hartford area within approximately a 2–3 mile radius is required. Skills: Strong communication skills and a professional, service-oriented demeanor when interacting with students, faculty, staff, and the public. Dependability: Reliable attendance and ability to follow schedules and directions. Physical: Ability to sit for extended periods as needed. Safe Transportation: Operate College shuttle vehicles, including 7-passenger mini-vans and 12-passenger transit vans, safely and in compliance with traffic laws and College policies. Shuttle Services: Operate College shuttle vehicles, including 7-passenger mini-vans and 12-passenger transit vans, safely and in compliance with traffic laws and College policies. Local Knowledge: Demonstrate knowledge of the Hartford area within approximately a 2–3 mile radius to determine safe and efficient routes and assist with directions when needed. Vehicle Inspections: Perform pre-trip and post-trip inspections, including checking lights, tires, fluid levels, and overall vehicle condition. Passenger Safety: Ensure passengers follow safety protocols, including seatbelt use and vehicle capacity limits. Reporting: Maintain accurate mileage logs and promptly report mechanical issues, damage, or incidents to the appropriate supervisor and Campus Safety. Customer Service: Provide professional, courteous, and respectful service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/102": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Director of Advancement Informations Systems",
      "description": "Department: Prospect Research & Information Systems Category: College Advancement JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States The Senior Associate Director of Advancement Information Systems leads advancement’s database operations, including data maintenance, and gift entry and workflow processes. Reporting to the Executive Director of Research, Prospect Management, Advancement Information Services & Database Management, the Associate Director ensures the accuracy, integrity, and usability of constituent and giving data and drives continuous improvement across systems, processes, documentation, and reporting tools that support fundraising, prospect management, and institutional decision-making. The Associate Director supervises three Gift Recording and Data Integrity Specialists and is accountable for workflow management, data quality, and team development, including recruiting, onboarding, training, coaching, and retention. This role exercises judgment in prioritizing work, resolving complex issues, and implementing solutions, and serves as a key liaison with Information Technology and Accounting Services to support system reliability, compliance, reconciliation, and strong customer service. The role is expected to identify issues proactively and implement solutions, consulting the Executive Director on strategic priorities and high-impact decisions. As the College advances its conversion to Slate CRM, the Associate Director proactively identifies and flags data and operational gaps to support successful implementation and continuity of service. Trinity College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, wellness, dental and vision, retirement savings with employer match, flexible spending and health savings accounts, disability and life insurance; paid leave and other paid time off benefits; tuition benefits for employees and their dependents; and a variety of other employer-sponsored and voluntary fringe benefit programs. The anticipated annual base salary hiring range for this position is $53,300 to $65,200 per year, with final placement determined by experience, skills, qualifications, and internal equity considerations. Bachelor's Degree 5-8 years of experience Experience leading gift entry/gift processing, including reconciliation with finance, and applying strong data integrity and quality control standards. Advancement Information Systems & Operational Leadership Lead the daily operations of the Advancement Information Systems (AIS) team. Establish and manage workflows, protocols, service standards, and internal controls for data, reporting, and gift processing functions that reflect best practices. Serve as the primary escalation point for complex AIS issues; assess root causes and implement solutions in coordination with key stakeholders. Evaluate AIS practices and partnerships and recommend improvements to strengthen efficiency, accuracy, and service quality. Support system readiness and continuity as Trinity advances its conversion to Slate CRM, proactively identifying and flagging operational and data-related gaps. Trinity College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, wellness, dental and vision, retirement savings with employer match, flexible spending and health savings accounts, disability and life insurance; paid leave and other paid time off benefits; tuition benefits for employees and their dependents; and a variety of other employer-sponsored and voluntary fringe benefit programs. The anticipated annual base salary hiring range for this position is $53,300 to $65,200 per year, with final placement determined by experience, skills, qualifications, and internal equity considerations. Team Supervision, Workflow Management & Staff Development Supervise three Gift Recording and Data Integrity Specialists, ensuring clear performance expectations, consistent accuracy, and high customer service standards. Manage workload distribution and workflow oversight to ensure timely completion of gift processing and data integrity tasks. Recruit, hire, onboard, train, and retain staff; provide coaching, performance feedback, and professional development support. Foster a collaborative, accountable team culture aligned with accuracy, responsiveness, and continuous improvement. Data Stewardship, Governance & Documentation Own and enforce data integrity standards, policies, and procedures for constituent and giving records in Slate. Develop and implement audits and quality checks to maintain data completeness, consistency, and reliability, minimizing institutional risk. Resolve complex constituent and gift record issues and provide standards-based guidance to advancement colleagues. Maintain and update policies, procedures, and training materials to ensure consistent application across the division. Reporting, Analytics & Information Delivery In collaboration with the director of database management, develop, maintain, and troubleshoot scheduled reports, dashboards, and recurring data outputs supporting fundraising, prospect management, reconciliation, and leadership decision-making. Identify trends, reporting gaps, and data concerns; propose and implement improvements to enhance decision support and operational effectiveness. Gift Entry, Reconciliation & Cross-Department Partnership Lead gift entry and gift processing workflows to ensure accurate, timely, and compliant recording of all contributions, including gifts, pledges, payments, matching gifts, adjustments, and complex transactions. Ensure appropriate crediting and documentation of donor intent; maintain compliance with gift acceptance policies, audit requirements, and reporting standards. Partner with Accounting Services to support reconciliation, resolve discrepancies, and ensure alignment between Advancement and Finance records. Serve as the operational liaison with Information Technology and Accounting Services regarding system functionality, integrations, access, and data flow concerns. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/103": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Department: Financial Aid Office Category: Admissions/Financial Aid JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Reporting to the Senior Associate Director of Financial Aid, the Financial Aid Counselor assists in upholding the highest levels of customer service to all Trinity students as it relates to institutional aid processes, timelines, and communication supporting the recruitment, enrollment, and retention of Trinity applicants and students. The Financial Aid Counselor is a key member of the enrollment team, utilizing broad knowledge of policy and practices in admissions and financial assistance. The position may often be the first point of contact with the college, and therefore, must become familiar with college personnel, operations, and events, and be capable of creating a positive first impression of the college. The Financial Aid Counselor will join a service-oriented team and is responsible for counseling students and parents in all areas of financial aid. Trinity College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, wellness, dental and vision, retirement savings with employer match, flexible spending and health savings accounts, disability and life insurance; paid leave and other paid time off benefits; tuition benefits for employees and their dependents; and a variety of other employer-sponsored and voluntary fringe benefit programs. The anticipated annual base salary hiring range for this position is $44,000 to $53,800 per year, with final placement determined by experience, skills, qualifications, and internal equity considerations. Bachelor's Degree 1-3 years of experience, required Possess strong computer skills, including Word, Excel, and other Microsoft Office programs. The ability to prioritize conflicting demands is essential, as is the ability to work effectively and comfortably with the public. Have a record of maintaining confidentiality, exercising discretion, and using good judgment. Must demonstrate the ability to anticipate and react appropriately to a variety of situations and to be resourceful. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Experience working in Financial Aid, especially with PowerFAIDS or Perceptive Content software. Proven organizational and administrative skills, and the ability to balance multiple priorities. Clear and effective writing, with knowledge of editorial procedures. Contribute to the recruitment and retention of all students by providing exemplary customer service, and counseling to students and families on eligibility guidelines for financial aid, application procedures, appeals, etc. Perform needs analysis, federal verification, and counsel a designated population of students on eligibility guidelines for financial aid, application procedures, and appeals. Remain abreast of all relevant government regulations and compliance guidelines related to financial assistance. Serve as an interdepartmental liaison reinforcing our commitment to student engagement, connection, and transformation. Execute the awarding of numerous internal and external grant and scholarship programs. Oversee, coordinate, and execute additional responsibilities for the Office of Financial Aid as assigned by office leadership. Prepare reports related to tasks assigned by Director or Associate Director of Financial Aid. Access PowerFAIDS, to support and facilitate the aid process. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/99": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Parent and Family Giving",
      "description": "Department: Parent & Family Giving Category: College Advancement JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College seeks a dynamic, relationship-driven Associate Director of Parent and Family Giving to help grow one of the College's most important philanthropic constituencies. Reporting to the Director of Parent and Family Giving, the Associate Director will cultivate, solicit, and steward parents and family members capable of making leadership and major gifts while helping execute a comprehensive engagement strategy for Trinity's parent community. The Associate Director will manage a portfolio of approximately 125 parent prospects and work closely with colleagues across Advancement to strengthen parent participation and inspire philanthropic investment in Trinity. This role offers an exciting opportunity to build meaningful relationships with families and play a critical role in advancing the College's priorities. Bachelor's Degree 1-3 years of experience Demonstrated ability to cultivate relationships and successfully solicit leadership or major gifts, or comparable experience. Outstanding oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently. Collaborative team player who enjoys working across departments to advance institutional goals. High degree of professionalism, integrity, initiative, and sound judgment. Computer fluency including Microsoft Office Suite, donor database software, and query tools. Appreciation for Trinity College's mission and the transformative impact of liberal arts education. Manage a portfolio of approximately 125 parent and family prospects through all stages of qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Develop and implement individualized strategies to secure leadership and major gifts in support of Trinity's highest priorities. Partner with the Director of Parent and Family Giving to identify and qualify new parent prospects and strengthen the overall parent giving pipeline. Assist in planning and executing parent engagement initiatives, including regional events, campus programs, and Parents Leadership Council activities. Collaborate with colleagues across Major Gifts, Annual Giving, Athletic Giving, Stewardship, Alumni Relations, and Principal Giving to deliver a coordinated parent engagement strategy. Prepare briefing materials, proposals, stewardship reports, and other donor communications to support successful fundraising Maintain accurate prospect records and timely documentation of donor interactions within the College's CRM. Travel regularly to cultivate and solicit prospects. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/101": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Advancement",
      "description": "Department: VP College Advancement Category: College Advancement JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College seeks a highly organized, service-oriented Administrative Assistant to provide administrative and operational support within the Advancement Office. This position works across the Advancement organization and provides support to multiple individuals and functions, requiring strong organizational skills, sound judgment, flexibility, and the ability to manage competing priorities. The Administrative Assistant serves as a professional and welcoming point of contact for colleagues, alumni, donors, students, families, and other members of the Trinity community. The successful candidate will demonstrate discretion in handling confidential information, excellent customer service skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Associate's Degree Bachelor's Degree , preferred 1-3 years of experience Experience as an administrative support team member Facility with technology. Organization and attention to detail: Maintains accurate records, follows through on assignments, and effectively manages multiple priorities. Confidentiality and discretion: Handles sensitive information appropriately and demonstrates sound professional judgment. Customer service: Provides responsive, courteous, and solutions-oriented service to internal and external constituents. Collaboration: Builds positive working relationships and effectively supports colleagues across the Advancement Office. Flexibility: Responds positively to changing priorities and is willing to assist where needed. Communication: Communicates clearly, professionally, and effectively in person, by phone, and in writing. Initiative: Anticipates needs, follows through on responsibilities, and identifies ways to improve administrative processes. Provide day-to-day administrative support to multiple members of the Advancement Office Manage and prioritize multiple assignments, deadlines, and requests while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Coordinate meetings, appointments, calendars, correspondence, and other administrative activities as needed. Prepare, format, proofread, and organize correspondence, reports, presentations, and other documents. Respond to inquiries and requests in a timely, courteous, and professional manner. Work efficiently in the CRM and other platforms used throughout the division."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/100": {
      "title": "HRIS Analyst",
      "description": "Department: Human Resources Category: Human Resources JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States The HRIS Analyst plays a critical role in managing HR systems, ensuring data integrity, and delivering actionable insights to support strategic HR initiatives. The role bridges HR and IT, focusing on system functionality, data integrity, and process improvement. This position combines technical expertise with analytical skills to optimize HR processes and enhance organizational effectiveness. High School Diploma or GED Bachelor's Degree, preferred 3-5 years of experience On-going Oracle Fusion HCM administration and configuration to support operations, system updates, and the release of new functionality Develop data management practices and audits to maintain high-quality data Report building and dashboard creation Serve as HR data subject matter expert for validation of external compliance reporting Act as a liaison to campus partners on the appropriate use and sharing of HR data Trinity workforce metrics and KPI development HR process knowledge across the employee lifecycle Understanding of AI applications in HR Project management Oracle HCM administration and configuration Data management and quality assurance HR Data & Reporting: Analyze workforce trends, maintain automated dashboards, and fulfill compliance reporting requirements. Compensation & Benefits Analytics: Provide salary benchmarking, equity analysis, and evaluate benefits utilization for cost-effectiveness. Talent & Organizational Insights: Track recruitment metrics, support performance review cycles, and assist with succession planning through data analysis. Compliance & Audit: Prepare documentation for audits and ensure adherence to institutional, federal, and state regulations. Training and education: Design and draft training and resource materials for human resources and community members to utilize HRIS systems to optimize system usage. Establish and maintain the data standards, validation rules, and audit practices governing core HR data in Oracle Cloud HCM; ensure HR data quality in partnership with TDI and represent the HR office on the College's data governance committee and related functions. Serve as the campus technical lead for Oracle Cloud HCM; translate functional requirements from HR and partner offices into sound system solutions; advise campus partners on system capability and constraints, and recommend business process best practices Assists with various projects, assigned by AVP of Human Resources Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/97": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Enrollment Experiences",
      "description": "Department: Admissions Office Category: Admissions/Financial Aid JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College seeks a creative, strategic, and collaborative professional to serve as Associate Director of Enrollment Experiences. This role is responsible for designing and delivering high-impact on-campus, off-campus, virtual, and hybrid experiences that engage prospective students, admitted students, families, high school counselors, and other key enrollment constituents. The Associate Director will ensure that every enrollment experience reflects Trinity’s brand, values, academic distinction, and commitment to student-centered engagement, helping position the College as a first-choice destination for students. Working strategically and diplomatically with faculty, facilities, student life, academic departments, and other campus stakeholders, this position will serve as an advocate for the enrollment team while building partnerships that support thoughtful, cohesive, and welcoming experiences across the enrollment funnel. This role requires a forward-thinking, solutions-oriented professional who can balance creativity with operational excellence, anticipate challenges, and collaborate effectively across the College to advance Trinity’s enrollment goals. Bachelor's Degree 3-5 years of experience 5-8 years of experience, preferred Strong event and experience design skills, with demonstrated ability to plan, execute, and assess high-impact programs. Excellent project management, organizational, and analytical skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines, stakeholders, and events in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail and ability to create polished, welcoming, inclusive, and brand-aligned experiences for guests. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to create event plans, schedules, briefings, communications, and follow-up materials for internal and external audiences. Ability to build productive relationships and collaborate effectively with various stakeholders and partners. Demonstrated ability to influence, coordinate, and lead cross-functional work without direct authority. Solid technological and data literacy, including experience or comfort with CRM systems, event platforms, survey tools virtual event platforms, spreadsheets, and data reporting. Ability to use data, feedback, and assessment results to evaluate visitor experiences and recommend improvements. Self-motivated, proactive, flexible, and solutions-oriented, with a history of meeting deadlines and managing complex projects independently. Ability and willingness to work evenings and weekends and to travel by car, plane, train or boat as needed for event planning logistics. Must have a valid motor vehicle license.​ Lead the vision, design, and execution of Trinity’s enrollment experiences, including daily visits, group visits, open houses, admitted student events, counselor programs, virtual offerings, and off-campus/regional events and experiences for enrollment constituents. Maintain CRM platform (Slate) as it relates to daily visits and group visits Serve as the primary point of contact for group visit requests Serve as the primary liaison for enrollment experiences with faculty, academic departments, facilities, student life, and other campus partners including but not limited to advancement/alumni relations, athletics, institutional events. Collect and analyze feedback, participation data, and engagement metrics. Use insights to recommend improvements and inform future planning. Prepare summaries and insights for enrollment leadership as needed. Provide guidance and support to colleagues including enrollment colleagues, faculty, and staff from other divisions across campus who contribute to enrollment events and visits. May supervise student employees May supervise professional staff"
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/84": {
      "title": "Seasonal Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Department: Athletics and Recreation Category: Athletics JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College in Hartford CT, an NCAA Division III, liberal arts and science college in the New England Small College Athletic Conference (NESCAC), is seeking to fill seasonal coach position for the Athletics division. Candidate will be expected to help the program continue to grow and build upon the program’s success. High School Diploma, GED Familiarity and/or interest with NCAA and NESCAC athletic operations. Coaching and teaching the skills, tactics and strategies while contributing to the overall development of NCAA student-athletes. Knowledge of and adherence to NESCAC and NCAA rules, recruiting, practice planning and execution, equipment maintenance, teaching responsibilities and mentoring student-athletes. The seasonal coach will be expected to help promote and facilitate the College and Athletic Department’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion initiatives. The seasonal coach will have administrative duties within the Department. This position requires both early morning and weekend availability throughout the academic year. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics"
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/83": {
      "title": "Director of Institutional Event Project Management",
      "description": "Department: Events & Campus Operations Category: Finance and Operations JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States The Director of Institutional Event Project Management serves as Trinity College's centralized project management leader for assigned institutional events. The Director provides strategic planning, project management, operational coordination, and continuous improvement for the College's highest-profile academic, ceremonial, presidential, and institutional events. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, administrators, and campus partners, the Director leads a standardized planning methodology that strengthens collaboration, promotes operational excellence, preserves institutional knowledge, and creates exceptional institutional experiences aligned with the College's mission and strategic priorities. Required Bachelor's Degree, required Five to seven years of progressively responsible experience in project management, institutional operations, higher education administration, event management, or related fields. Demonstrated success managing complex, cross-functional projects. Excellent organizational and project management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Experience facilitating collaborative planning processes. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Preferred Master's Degree, preferred Experience in higher education. Experience managing major institutional events, commencements, convocations, or presidential events. Knowledge of project management methodologies. Experience with enterprise scheduling or event management systems (EMS or similar). Familiarity with higher education governance and academic protocol. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strategic planning Project management Operational integration Facilitation and consensus building Organizational leadership Executive communication Risk management Budget awareness Process improvement Data analysis and reporting Customer service and hospitality Continuous improvement Institutional Project Management Lead comprehensive project management for assigned institutional events. Develop and maintain master project plans and implementation schedules. Coordinate planning timelines, milestones, and deliverables. Monitor project progress and facilitate timely decision-making. Identify project risks and develop mitigation strategies. Ensure alignment with institutional priorities and strategic objectives. Cross-Functional Planning & Coordination Coordinate planning across multiple College divisions and departments. Facilitate Institutional Events Team meetings. Build collaborative relationships among campus partners. Coordinate planning activities across all Institutional Planning Areas. Ensure effective communication among stakeholders. Support Executive Sponsors throughout the planning process. Operational Readiness Lead Operational Readiness Reviews for institutional events. Coordinate venue readiness, logistics, technology, hospitality, safety, and campus presentation. Monitor event readiness and resolve operational issues. Coordinate event-day operations and decision support. Ensure contingency and emergency plans are in place. Planning Methodology & Standards Implement and maintain Trinity College's Institutional Experiences and Event Management Framework. Develop and continuously improve planning templates, project documentation, and operational standards. Maintain planning calendars and project management tools. Promote consistent planning practices across institutional events. Support organizational learning and planning excellence Assessment & Continuous Improvement Lead structured post-event assessments. Measure operational performance and institutional outcomes. Capture lessons learned and best practices. Maintain institutional planning documentation. Recommend improvements to planning processes and participant experiences. Prepare executive reports and recommendations. Executive Support Prepare planning briefings and executive updates. Support senior leadership with planning analysis and recommendations. Coordinate materials for Executive Sponsors and College leadership. Assist with strategic decision-making throughout the planning process. Institutional Planning Areas Coordinate planning across the College's Institutional Planning Areas, including: Academic & Ceremony Operations Student Experience & Engagement Operations & Logistics Facilities & Infrastructure Safety & Emergency Management Communications & Marketing Information Technology & Event Production Hospitality & Guest Experience Advancement & Constituent Engagement Trinity Traditions & Institutional Heritage Presidential & Executive Engagement Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/79": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach (Women's Squash)",
      "description": "Department: Athletics Category: Athletics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College in Hartford CT, an NCAA Division III, liberal arts and science college in the New England Small College Athletic Conference (NESCAC), is seeking to fill a full-time assistant coach position for our Women's Squash program. Candidate will be expected to help the program continue to grow and build upon the program’s success. The primary function of this role is coaching and teaching the sport of Squash. High School Diploma, GED Playing and/or coaching experience in Squash Familiarity and/or interest with NCAA and NESCAC athletic operations. Coaching and teaching the skills, tactics and strategies of Women's Squash while contributing to the overall development of NCAA student-athletes. Assisting the head coach in leading and organizing all facets of a varsity Women's Squash program. Knowledge of and adherence to NESCAC and NCAA rules, recruiting, practice planning and execution, equipment maintenance, teaching responsibilities and mentoring student-athletes. The assistant coach will be expected to help promote and facilitate the College and Athletic Department’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion initiatives. The assistant coach will have administrative duties within the Department. This position requires both early morning and weekend availability throughout the academic year. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics"
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/71": {
      "title": "Director of Bantam Network and Residential Experience",
      "description": "Department: Bantam Network Residential Learning Community Category: Student & Community Life JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Lead the Bantam Network which works to honor the holistic nature of the student within Residence Life and Housing. Oversee a staff of five to cultivate opportunities that contribute to our students’ academic, social, personal, and professional development and growth, as they move through their Trinity experience. Promote an environment that provides students with a diverse, inclusive, and caring living-learning community. To uphold this commitment, all professional staff live in residence with our students. Most importantly, the director focuses on further developing and strengthening the Network as a resource for students across all four years of their Trinity experience, helping guide students through their college journey. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education. 5 or more years of post-baccalaureate professional experience in housing operations, residential life, or student support services. Demonstrated competence in leadership and administration, Student Affairs theory and practice, policy development and budget management. Advanced knowledge of housing operations (including assignments and facilities), care and crisis management, advising and/or counseling techniques, and student support services. Extensive expertise in housing assignment software, such as eRezLife and StarRez. Proven experience in implementing and assessing a Residential Curriculum programming model on a college campus. Working knowledge of applicable laws and regulations related to housing, student records, and student accommodations including, FERPA, Title IX, Clery Act, Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), etc. Ability to work independently with limited supervision; ability to work effectively with students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in student Affairs/Higher Education, College Student Personnel, Counseling, or related field. 5 years of post-master’s progressive experience in housing operations or residential life in a higher education setting. Experience serving the needs of students from a range of backgrounds to determine reasonable accommodations to meet students’ diverse needs. Skilled in analyzing, interpreting, and incorporating applicable laws, regulations, policies, and practices related to housing, student records, and student accommodations, and practices in daily work activities and decision-making to meet the needs of students. This includes FERPA, Title IX, Clery Act, Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), etc. Knowledge of principles and procedures involved in risk assessment in a college setting. Adept at supervision, strategic planning, assessment of programs and services, budget, and resource management; strong organizational skills with attention to detail and ability to set priorities and meet deadlines. Excellent oral and written communication skills, coupled with the ability to work effectively with diverse students, faculty, staff, administrators, parents/guardians; excellent interpersonal skills, ability to build and sustain relationships with all stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to work well independently and with limited supervision; skilled in exercising judgment necessary to deal with confidential and sensitive information and to respond to complex student emergencies, providing appropriate intervention and referral. On-call experience, managing student/ facilities incidents on a college campus. The Director of the Bantam Network and Residential Experience will fulfill the following facets of the role: Operation and Administration: Serve as a leader with primary responsibility for the residential facilities, operational and programmatic efforts to provide safe, healthy, inclusive on-campus housing for students that promotes learning, personal development, and academic achievement. Strategic Planning and Assessment: Work with campus partners to create a campus culture that promotes character, ethical development and civic responsibility. Promote awareness of campus policies and procedures regarding student conduct and expectations. Advance the mission, values, and strategic priorities of the College and the Division through goals and initiatives that emphasize care, wellbeing support, mentorship, belonging, and community engagement for students and maximizing staff capacity through streamlined operations, engagement, and communication. Leadership and Supervision: Lead Housing and the Residential Experience, overseeing personnel, budgets, Housing Operations and Assignments, the Residential Curriculum, and Residential Facilities. Collaborative Partnerships: Develop, implement, and collaborate with key campus partners on high-level events, programs, and initiatives relevant to housing and the residential experience."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/54": {
      "title": "Global Engagement Advisor",
      "description": "Department: Global Engagement Office (GEO) Category: Academic Affairs (non-faculty) JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States The Global Engagement Advisor is an inaugural, dual-role position that bridges the regulatory and advising functions of the Office of International Students and Scholars (OISS) with the student engagement and program operations of the Global Engagement Office (formerly the Office of Study Away). We are seeking an adaptable, collaborative professional who brings a student-centered approach to both advising and programming. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, enjoys wearing multiple hats, and is passionate about supporting students from around the world. As a key member of our team, the Advisor will lead the “front door” of the office—creating a welcoming, inclusive experience through front-desk management, student staff supervision, and thoughtful, academically intentional advising and engagement. U.S. Citizenship or Lawful Permanent Residency (required for DSO/ARO eligibility under federal law) Bachelor’s degree and 3–5 years of relevant professional experience in international education, advising, student support, or program coordination Demonstrated ability to be flexible, adaptable, and resourceful in a dynamic work environment Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work both independently and across departments High attention to detail, excellent time management, & strong organizational skills Experience working with SEVIS Commitment to inclusive, student-centered practices and cross-cultural engagement Preferred Master's Degree in International Education, Higher Education Administration, or related field Experience with both international student advising and study abroad administration Familiarity with design tools such as Canva Experience with application management systems such as Terra Dotta or Horizons Under the guidance of the Associate Director for Global Engagement and the Associate Director for International Students and Scholars, responsibilities include: Under the direction of the Associate Director, support the strategic shift from individual advising appointments to a layered, holistic, student-centered approach. Prioritize peer-led group-based engagement with a focus on academic integration. In collaboration with the Associate Directors, coordinate and support global learning and outreach initiatives (on and off campus) such as study abroad fairs, information sessions, and classroom visits. Lead engagement programs like Global Talks and International Student Orientation to foster meaningful connections between international students, campus, and the local community. Occasional travel required to partner schools, fairs, and professional conferences. Serve as the primary point of contact for Global Engagement Program Providers (GEP), offering recruitment support, and troubleshooting assistance for students during the application, and onboarding process. Manage daily front-desk operations and oversee the shared office email account, ensuring responsive, student-friendly communication and a welcoming environment. Assist with the development of key marketing materials and brand formatting. Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO), issuing Form I-20s and maintaining accurate records in SEVIS. Serve as a back-up to the Primary Designated School Official (PDSO) as needed for occasional coverage and emergencies. Monitor and interpret federal regulations related to international students and travel, serving as a knowledgeable resource and backup to the Primary DSO. Recruit, train, and supervise Global Engagement Peer Mentors to serve as the first point of contact for all students. Establish tiered referral processes to resolve advanced student cases. Oversee mentor-mentee matching, with a focus on building an inclusive and supportive student community. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental needs."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/68": {
      "title": "Assistant Softball Coach",
      "description": "Department: Athletics Category: Athletics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College in Hartford CT, an NCAA Division III, liberal arts and science college in the New England Small College Athletic Conference (NESCAC), is seeking to fill a full-time assistant coach position for our Softball program. Candidate will be expected to help the program continue to grow and build upon the program’s success. The primary function of this role is coaching and teaching the sport of Softball. In addition, the Assistant Coach will serve as acting Head Coach for an anticipated period of approximately 15 weeks to provide leadership and continuity during a temporary leave. High School Diploma, or GED Bachelor's Degree, preferred Playing and/or coaching experience in Softball Familiarity and/or interest with NCAA and NESCAC athletic operations Coaching and teaching the skills, tactics and strategies of [SPORT] while contributing to the overall development of NCAA student-athletes. Assisting the head coach in leading and organizing all facets of a varsity [SPORT] program. Knowledge of and adherence to NESCAC and NCAA rules, recruiting, practice planning and execution, equipment maintenance, teaching responsibilities and mentoring student-athletes. The assistant coach will be expected to help promote and facilitate the College and Athletic Department’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion initiatives. The assistant coach will have administrative duties within the Department. This position requires both early morning and weekend availability throughout the academic year. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics"
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/70": {
      "title": "Residential Learning Coordinator",
      "description": "Department: Residential Services Category: Student & Community Life JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Under the leadership of the Director and the Associate Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Residential Learning Coordinator (RLC) oversees multiple residential communities within the Trinity College Housing system. The Residential Learning Coordinator position is a crucial role within Housing and Residence Life, and this position is responsible for creating, facilitating, and assessing programs, initiatives, and administrative policies that align with the mission of the department. RLCs report to the Associate Director. This is an in-person, 12-month live-in position. The Residential Learning Coordinator works to foster an inclusive living and learning community that contributes to students’ academic achievement and personal growth. Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree, preferred 1-3 years of experience Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to work well in fast-paced and stressful environments Good time management skills with the ability to prioritize work Exceptional human relations/customer service skills with the ability to respond effectively to sensitive inquiries or complaints Ability to work independently as well as with a team Exceptional communication (written and oral) skills Skill in program planning, implementation, and management, including budgeting Ability to train team members or student employees and schedule/coordinate work and activities of others Ability to cultivate and maintain relationships with leadership, faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders/constituencies Administrative Processes Manage the daily operations of designated residential communities while partnering with essential campus colleagues, including facilities, to maintain a clean and safe living environment for our students. Participate in an out-of-hours on-call rotation and serve as a member of the crisis response team, which may include hospital visits to check on students outside of traditional business hours. Play an essential role in implementing the department's Residential Curriculum, ensuring that our students have the chance to engage with the broader campus community and its resources. Oversee program requests and program implementation from Resident Staff including Resident Advisors (RAs) and Community Assistants (CAs). Manage the budget for the resident staff programs. Collaborate with members of the campus community to provide students with holistic programs and support services. Oversee social media pages. Participate as needed in corresponding with students in the general housing inbox. Student Support Services Work collaboratively with the deans of Student and Community Life, along with faculty to provide support and guidance for students. Meet with students to discuss their needs and connect them to campus resources and support services. Conduct residential well-being checks on students as needed. Evaluate and manage conduct and wellbeing cases in accordance with college policies, utilizing our conduct software, Maxient. Assess behavioral and educational sanctions for policy violations while offering guidance, mediation, and problem-solving. Respond to student/parent concerns that arise either via email, phone, or in person. Collaborative Partnerships Collaborate with members of the campus community to provide students with holistic programs and support services. Gain broad experience in higher-education administration by partnering with colleagues from across campus to help students transition and acclimate to Trinity, as well as learn about opportunities while enrolled. Serve on committees as requested. The ideal candidate is expected to have broad and relevant experience in residential life, activities planning, student advising/mentoring, and student leadership development. A good understanding of liberal arts communities is preferred. Candidates should have a passion for mentorship and deliberate interaction with students."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/45": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach (Field Hockey)",
      "description": "Department: Athletics Category: Athletics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College in Hartford CT, an NCAA Division III, liberal arts and science college in the New England Small College Athletic Conference (NESCAC), is seeking to fill a full-time assistant coach position for our Field Hockey program. Candidate will be expected to help the program continue to grow and build upon the program’s success. The primary function of this role is coaching and teaching the sport of Field Hockey. High School Diploma or GED, required Bachelor's Degree, preferred Familiarity and/or interest with NCAA and NESCAC athletic operations. Coaching and teaching the skills, tactics and strategies of Field Hockey while contributing to the overall development of NCAA student-athletes. Assisting the head coach in leading and organizing all facets of a varsity Field Hockey program. Knowledge of and adherence to NESCAC and NCAA rules, recruiting, practice planning and execution, equipment maintenance, teaching responsibilities and mentoring student-athletes. The assistant coach will be expected to help promote and facilitate the College and Athletic Department’s commitment to Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion initiatives. The assistant coach will have administrative duties within the Department. This position requires both early morning and weekend availability throughout the academic year. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics"
