    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/28": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Department: Campus Safety Category: Campus Safety JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States ​​Safeguard the campus through regular patrols and extensive interaction and partnerships with students, faculty, staff, visitors, and the broader Hartford community. Support a positive student experience by creating a safe and inclusive campus environment and enforcing college policies and community standards. Help perform incident investigations and respond to emergencies and crises on campus.​ High School Diploma or GED Associates, preferred 1-3 years of work experience ​​Driver’s License and excellent driving record ​Able to pass a background investigation ​​Experience/commitment to working with and supporting diverse communities ​Possess strong critical thinking skills ​Ability to handle sensitive and challenging situations with professionalism and compassion ​Ability to work effectively and collaboratively as a member of a diverse team ​Display sensitivity to the unique role that security plays in a college setting ​Effective oral and written communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills ​Strong conflict resolution, negotiation, collaboration, and facilitation skills and experience ​Computer and written skills consistent with the completion of detailed and comprehensive reports on computer-based reporting systems ​Meticulous attention to detail ​Reliable and able to work independently under established guidelines ​Able to perform duties at night and during inclement weather ​Previous campus safety experience is a plus ​Ability to speak a second language is a plus​ Conduct active and random patrols of the campus to provide a safe and secure environment for individuals and property, and to enforce college policies and community standards​ ​​Perform initial investigations of incidents, conduct follow-up investigations, and make accurate and timely written reports​ Respond to emergencies, problems and complaints, and provide care and resources to those who are sick, injured, or in crisis​ ​​Perform duties in uniform and may travel by foot, bicycle, or marked Campus Safety Vehicle​ Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental needs"
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Department: Campus Safety Category: Campus Safety JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States ​ ​ The Dispatcher will serve as the initial point of contact for Campus Safety services, providing communications for department services. The position will dispatch Campus Safety Officers for routine and emergency situations and receive incoming communications via telephone, web-based alerts, or radio relating to Campus Safety services. ​ ​ High School Diploma or GED ​ ​ 1-3 Years ​ of work experience ​Preferred: 2 years Campus Safety environment, prior public safety or emergency dispatch experience is highly preferred ​ Serve as the initial point of contact for Campus Safety services, handling calls for service, general inquiries, and other requests with professionalism, empathy, and compassion ​ ​ ​ Assist a diverse campus community of students, faculty, and staff through a customer-centric approach while working in the dispatch center ​ ​ ​ Receive incoming communication relating to Campus Safety services of the college and operate the Campus Safety radio communication system to dispatch personnel for performance of duties. Support flow of information to personnel including information from outside law enforcement agencies and receive emergency alarms. Keep supervisors informed of all incidents and make appropriate notification of on-call personnel based upon published lists ​ ​ Maintain or monitor relevant computer databases and reporting systems during assigned tour including entering incident data, monitoring safety device and access system software, and Blue light emergency phone network ​ ​ Proactively monitor a robust video surveillance system to deter crime, inform patrols of suspicious activity, and research unfolding or recent events ​ ​ Monitor the Campus Safety office during assigned shifts, addressing walk-in inquiries, requests for service, and related administrative tasks ​ ​ Maintain, and be able to access, critical information related to college operations such as: daily schedules, policies, and bulletins, daily crime log, Clery Act log, vehicle tow logs, campus community member contact records, and blue light emergency phones ​ Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental needs"
    }
